{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress","id":1190751,"title":"What if all the Solars were released before the disappearance of the Empress?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-01T12:49:02-08:00","id":1190751,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What if all the Solars were released before the disappearance of the Empress?","content":"Idle thought here, what would happen if the Jade Prison was destroyed before the Empress disappeared? Some conditions:<br /> <br /> (1) The timeline is say 200 to 300 years before her official disappearance.<br /> (2) Use lore for any edition as appropriate. I think the answers will by and large be similar anyway.<br /> (3) Assume the Empress does not disappear<br /> (4) Likely, but not necessarily, no Infernals or Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 10-20-2023, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T12:52:49-08:00","id":1190752,"title":"","content":"Hmmmmm... I know this isn't really what you're asking, but was the Jade Prison destroyed before the Empress disappeared anyway?<br /> I mean, they happened at around the same time. Does the book say which happened first?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:17:21-08:00","id":1190763,"title":"","content":"The Solars still present a crisis to the Realm, but it's one that they can present a more unified response to.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm seeing legions moving throughout the Threshold, in constant battle with the endeavours of Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:21:03-08:00","id":1190764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1190763#post1190763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solars still present a crisis to the Realm, but it's one that they can present a more unified response to.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm seeing legions moving throughout the Threshold, in constant battle with the endeavours of Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This<br /> <br /> The wyld hunts will be well funded, Peleps Deled will not be in charge of the wyld hunt, and all Solars and Lunars will have to watch their backs constantly - or seek refuge in the bordermarshes where the Sids can't track them.<br /> <br /> Remember - the gold faction of the sids basically only rose up due to the resurgence of the solars - so all the sids would be united under Ketchup Karjack","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:27:16-08:00","id":1190767,"title":"","content":"But wouldn't the resurgence of the Solars embolden the Gold Faction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:35:53-08:00","id":1190770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1190764#post1190764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars will have to watch their backs constantly</div> </div> </div> </div>That's nothing new for the Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200bA stronger Realm response would change the manner of Solar adventures, but Solars are still strong, and it's a sudden increase beyond what the Realm has provisioned to deal with; hardly enough to say that all Solars are on the run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the gold faction of the sids basically only rose up due to the resurgence of the solars - so all the sids would be united under Ketchup Karjack</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Solars haven't resurged?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:47:27-08:00","id":1190774,"title":"","content":"Read first post again sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:58:46-08:00","id":1190778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1190764#post1190764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This<br /> <br /> The wyld hunts will be well funded, <b>Peleps Deled will not be in charge of the wyld hunt</b>, and all Solars and Lunars will have to watch their backs constantly - or seek refuge in the bordermarshes where the Sids can't track them.<br /> <br /> Remember - the gold faction of the sids basically only rose up due to the resurgence of the solars - so all the sids would be united under Ketchup Karjack</div> </div> </div> </div>He isn't now. He's just the head of a chapter house. Cathak Setod runs the overall show in the Office of Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T14:17:46-08:00","id":1190791,"title":"","content":"Depends. The appearance of the Solars earlier on in the Realm's dynastic culture, before the political culture had reached its pitch of intraelite competition, might have had a unifying effect; the Empress simply couldn't afford internal divide-and-rule competition to keep her Throne safe, and would have to settle on some form of defined mechanism to manage succession and mitigate feuding and competition, and the Houses would have to more or less accept it.<br /> <br /> If you avoid the incipient Civil War, you also tend to retain the (at least 1e) Realm-under-the-Empress's policies of relatively light extraction from satrapies and tributaries to prevent rebellion and maintain a sustainable revenue stream, and you avoid the heavy intra-House competition that is driving higher levels of extraction that are unsustainable, risk major rebellion and have led to open rebellion and declaration of independence among satrapies and tributaries in RY768. (At the same time as the Houses withdraw their troops in preparation for civil war conflict, further encouraging rebellion).<br /> <br /> (Another effect would be that, if we assume the Realm has been losing a stock of First Age magic since the founding of the Realm, they'd likely have a stronger artefact base to use.)<br /> <br /> On the contrary though, we have to consider what competitive multiple fronts tend to do to empires. There's some recent work in historical economics that posits that the Han Empire was reunified when the Roman wasn't because, though the Han Empire faced threats at least as dire as the Romans, they all tended to come from one direction, the northern steppes, while the Romans faced threats in almost every province to some degree. <br /> <br /> This tended to encourage the Chinese to maintain unity, to build a strong defensive line in one place, to save the entire North Chinese plain, and then the commanders of the forces here would dominate the rest of the country. While in the Roman case, because the threats were so disparate and from so many directions, and geography allowed lots of provinces to hold their own &quot;strong lines&quot; at different locations, the Empire tended to be broken up into regions, which in time evolved towards region states.<br /> <br /> Assuming all this, the Blessed Isle has something more of the Roman case about it, because surrounded by an entire Threshold of potential threats. So it might be that the Realm as it is (centered on the Isle, with significant colonial possessions across the world and centered in the near Threshold) tends to simply be unsustainable in the face of a Threshold that's not vastly militarily weaker as a whole, and the Realm has to either retreat to regional states of just the Isle itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T14:27:20-08:00","id":1190797,"title":"","content":"I am wondering about an additional question in extendtion to the first. <br /> <br /> Given a more unified and effective respons from the Realm. Would that provide the sids enough room and time to find Another way to lock solars up? Like finding the hosts of solar exaltation and keep them in controlled and subdued artficial suspension? <br /> <br /> Like drugs, otherwordly prisons or being dreameaten by the fae. Just Some examples","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T15:30:34-08:00","id":1190823,"title":"","content":"Does the Empress still vanish for reasons unknown? Cause part of the problem the Realm has is that her Redness being gone without a proper chain of succession leading to house infighting and a lack of anyone to rein in the more dangerously destructive aspects of inter house conflicts. Measures taken due to a massive solar resurgence would probably lessen the damage in points, but I still see the battle of futile blood including a few other houses taking the opportunity to cripple Tepet even if they don't take the same extent that happened in the normal setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T15:39:05-08:00","id":1190828,"title":"","content":"Hmm, if it's that far back, the makeup of the Great Houses is going to be quite a bit different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T16:00:21-08:00","id":1190831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1190764#post1190764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember - the gold faction of the sids basically only rose up due to the resurgence of the solars - so all the sids would be united under Ketchup Karjack</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a 3E change? Because the Sidereals have had several factions debating the Solar issue since the Usurpation. Several Sidereals that supported the Solars were killed as well, including Ayesha Ura's (Gold Faction leader) previous incarnation. There has never been a unified faction under Kejack... unless this is a 3E retcon I missed!?<br /> <br /> As for the OP's question, the Wyld Hunt would be far better staffed and funded. But it would still be extremely difficult for them to deal with the resurgence. The Empire is at war with the Lunar's in the Caul, they've only ever needed to track down 2-3 Solar's a decade in the past, and they've continuously failed to conquer the River Provinces. A sudden resurgence of 300 Solars would put a lot of pressure on the Empire. Solar's themselves would definitely have a greater threat against them, but the Shogunate is gone. The number of Dragonbloods is a fraction of what it was during the Usurpation. Honestly, between the Solars and Lunars (who reincarnate) and the Dragonbloods (requiring hereditary genetics), the Empire could lose on simple attrition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 03-01-2018, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T16:33:14-08:00","id":1190842,"title":"","content":"Great thoughts everyone! Just in case anyone missed my edits to the original post:<br /> <br /> (1) I'm thinking... say 300 years before her official disappearance.<br /> <br /> (2) I'm leaving edition aside - people can answer to whichever they find appropriate, I think the answers will by and large be similar anyway.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of greater pressure on the empire would be significant. As well, the solars would not necessarily be united either. Borked 2E population dynamics aside, I think DB's would be under considerably more pressure over time to have much larger families in order to make up for the attrition and losses to Solars in the Threshold.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T16:37:41-08:00","id":1190843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1190831#post1190831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless this is a 3E retcon I missed!?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think retcon isn't the right term to use, since it's an Edition starting from the beginning; it's not like when Masters of Jade retroactively had it that Liminals had always been there.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, to me, the description of Sidereals in the core book suggested that dividing around an active question about the place of Solars in Creation's future was only something that came up when there were actual Solars around.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T17:07:31-08:00","id":1190853,"title":"","content":"Now a fair question on the Gold Faction would be how much stronger or weaker would it be if the solars started being a thing that far back?<br /> <br /> I mean The Empress being gone and The Realm destabilizing has to be a major point in the current Sid decision on whether you stand with bronze or gold. I mean Sids have a lot of issues to deal with so where one stands on trying to become the power behind the new solar throne, or you know rage, fight, and struggle as hard as possible against the people trying to make that throne. If the Solars regained their full numbers (as the hypothetical is so far that Abyssals and Infernals will have different origins or not exist) and the Realm was as stable as it ever was then some are probably going to side with The Realm on the grounds that they would have to topple or overthrow it to put the Solars in charge. Though 300 years without the Solars going away, the second breath being taken where it may, the increase in survivors due to numbers alone would up mentors and Solar competency. Not to mention what happens every time a Dynast becomes a Solar and isn't put down you end up with a not inconsiderate amount of resources lost and potential secrets and things that have to be taken care of. After a time how many Sids might become in favor of Solars just because of all they've seen a Solar do and the fear that the Solars winning isn't so much a possibility, but an inevitability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T18:16:28-08:00","id":1190866,"title":"","content":"I propose that one can put a mass return of the Solars at any point after the Great Contagion, and the idea that switching control of the Realm turned out to be a bad move would be a credible position for a number of Sidereals.<br /> <br /> \u200bMaybe it's more, maybe it's less, but there's so few of them that I think it would be a difference in the single digits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T01:19:07-08:00","id":1190921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1190831#post1190831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The number of Dragonbloods is a fraction of what it was during the Usurpation. Honestly, between the Solars and Lunars (who reincarnate) and the Dragonbloods (requiring hereditary genetics), the Empire could lose on simple attrition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even this, though kind of depends on our assumptions about long it takes for Solars and Lunars to be &quot;reborn&quot; after death. It could take a generation for each slain Celestial to reincarnate.<br /> <br /> Getting bogged down in cross edition stuff, 1e Sidereals brought in the idea that Sidereal Exaltations take at least about the time of a child to be born and grow to maturity to be reborn; this then had the contrasting effect of implying that other Celestials were reborn almost instantly, even though this has never really been defined in the setting. Then people combined that with the idea that Solars learn and &quot;grow&quot; really quickly to sort of get at this idea that the Solars and Lunars were designed to be &quot;respawning&quot; heroes fighting a war of attrition that allowed them to overwhelm enemies that way (specifically the old Primordials). In the extreme its almost a sort of Agents from the Matrix sort of feel in which Dragonblooded fighting them find that if they actually manage to defeat one in close combat, the Exaltation will simply quickly possess another hero of equal quality immediately, and the Wyld Hunt is sort of like playing Whack-A-Mole.<br /> <br /> Some people did like this, in hindsight I do feel it was a bit unfortunate. I would prefer to sort of get away from this in favour of the idea that people truly don't know how long it will take for a Solar / Lunar to be reborn; each of them are special heroes with unique talents and each death is a great loss, which will return to the world someday, but where no one knows how long the world will have to wait (it could be a year, it could be thirty or more). This places more emphasis on their training and survival and on them as a precious resource, and that they have to win through smart tactics and survival rather than through attrition and Pyrrhic Defeats.<br /> <br /> (It's also more like the &quot;Falling in love&quot; analogy for Exaltation as well I guess. You don't just fall another person immediately after losing your partner, right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T05:31:00-08:00","id":1190952,"title":"","content":"I think it's the kind of thing that is best suited by the setting not heavily specifying, even if I think the examples lean a bit towards quicker reincarnation times, if only in service of the idea that there aren't going to be large gaps in the numbers of Exalted for decades.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy own biases are also kind of in favour of the idea that there's a certain expendability to the Exalted; that your player character is in fact not so special and rare and unique as to be completely irreplaceable in this generation. If nothing else, it makes it easier to describe them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1190921#post1190921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It's also more like the &quot;Falling in love&quot; analogy for Exaltation as well I guess. You don't just fall another person immediately after losing your partner, right?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T06:55:10-08:00","id":1190965,"title":"","content":"Maybe you could say that the Sun has an urge to exalt people, and the less solars there are, the looser his standards get. <br /> <br /> When there's 300 or so he'll go for a 10, but with a scant dozen he'll settle for a 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T07:04:54-08:00","id":1190970,"title":"","content":"When did Joachim live? If he had a source of young Solars he could have build a power base the empress would need an entire house or defense grid strike to take care off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T14:47:00-08:00","id":1191131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1190921#post1190921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even this, though kind of depends on our assumptions about long it takes for Solars and Lunars to be &quot;reborn&quot; after death. It could take a generation for each slain Celestial to reincarnate.<br /> <br /> Getting bogged down in cross edition stuff, 1e Sidereals brought in the idea that Sidereal Exaltations take at least about the time of a child to be born and grow to maturity to be reborn; this then had the contrasting effect of implying that other Celestials were reborn almost instantly, even though this has never really been defined in the setting. Then people combined that with the idea that Solars learn and &quot;grow&quot; really quickly to sort of get at this idea that the Solars and Lunars were designed to be &quot;respawning&quot; heroes fighting a war of attrition that allowed them to overwhelm enemies that way (specifically the old Primordials). In the extreme its almost a sort of Agents from the Matrix sort of feel in which Dragonblooded fighting them find that if they actually manage to defeat one in close combat, the Exaltation will simply quickly possess another hero of equal quality immediately, and the Wyld Hunt is sort of like playing Whack-A-Mole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I stated the Empire &quot;could&quot; lose a war of attrition, not that they would. There are a lot of variables to consider before digging into that scenario. However, 3E does present some facts that really limit the Dragonbloods ability to fight such a war. Such as it takes Dragonblood's decades between having children to recharge their &quot;mojo&quot;. It doesn't matter if it takes Solars/Lunars 10-20 years to reincarnate, it takes just as long for a Dragonblood to produce a child with a decent chance to exalt (and even that's not guaranteed).<br /> <br /> Also, we don't have any idea what the turn-around is for Solar/Lunar exalts once they're killed. What we do know is that dozens of Solars returned in the first couple of years after the Jade Prison was broken, and that's with only half of the Exaltations returning to the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> The other thing to consider is loss ratio. Solar's who join together and pool their resources provide a terrifying force multiplier. The Bull of the North pulled together a full circle of Solars, and devastated the Tepet legions. House Tepet lost so many terrestrial exalts that they're adopting almost every lost egg and exile they can find in an attempt to recover even a portion of their strength. All of that loss, and they only managed to kill 2 of the Solar's in the Bull's circle. That's not a sustainable loss ratio for the Empire.<br /> <br /> The Empress remaining on scene provides a great deal of stability for the Empire. However, the Wyld Hunt was designed to track down lone Solars and kill them before they developed their abilities. Even with the Empress maintaining support, the Wyld Hunt isn't ready to start taking on groups of Solars who have learned just what they're capable of doing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T15:29:03-08:00","id":1191146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1190952#post1190952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's the kind of thing that is best suited by the setting not heavily specifying</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, certainly I'm commenting here in the spirit of &quot;Let's examine our own assumptions about why we might have or not have reason to believe this is the case&quot; than attempt to hammer down my own preferences into the firmament.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1190952#post1190952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people do.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Implied judgmental puritanical frowning at such people. Unseriously.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T15:34:40-08:00","id":1191148,"title":"","content":"To be fair I don't think it takes decades for exaltations to pass as a rule. If we're assuming there was any attempt to balance how long it takes for a new celestial to be created vs how long for a new DB then the fact that DBs can increase their numbers would probably be a not inconsequential factor in that. I mean solars can never field a thousand of themselves, but the DBs have been building up their numbers. <br /> <br /> As far as turn around on exaltation goes for Solars and Lunars I'm thinking its kind of known as a thing that takes random time frames. I mean I wouldn't say it is a common thing for say a Lunar to die against a Wyld hunt and then the Lunar's pupil or someone in the hunt exalts almost immediately, but I wouldn't say it isn't unheard of as like a nightmare scenario. You know, &quot;Be vigilant its not unheard of for one of these monsters to wait until the first has been vanquished to strike when everyone's defenses are down. If any of you are unsure in the strength of your faith speak now and step away. It's better for your soul than risking the demon taking you over in the heat of the battle. It is, thankfully, a rare occurrence but it has been recorded.&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T15:11:24-08:00","id":1191458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1191148#post1191148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair I don't think it takes decades for exaltations to pass as a rule. If we're assuming there was any attempt to balance how long it takes for a new celestial to be created vs how long for a new DB then the fact that DBs can increase their numbers would probably be a not inconsequential factor in that. I mean solars can never field a thousand of themselves, but the DBs have been building up their numbers.<br /> <br /> As far as turn around on exaltation goes for Solars and Lunars I'm thinking its kind of known as a thing that takes random time frames. I mean I wouldn't say it is a common thing for say a Lunar to die against a Wyld hunt and then the Lunar's pupil or someone in the hunt exalts almost immediately, but I wouldn't say it isn't unheard of as like a nightmare scenario. You know, &quot;Be vigilant its not unheard of for one of these monsters to wait until the first has been vanquished to strike when everyone's defenses are down. If any of you are unsure in the strength of your faith speak now and step away. It's better for your soul than risking the demon taking you over in the heat of the battle. It is, thankfully, a rare occurrence but it has been recorded.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a pretty epic character background - being a Mortal warrior for the Hunt and Exalted moments after killing the Solar/Lunar.<br /> <br /> I think the idea that the Solars would grind down on the Realm's ability to control it's Tributaries in the Threshold as highly accurate/probable. Not to mention the Solars Exalting now and then inside the Realm to boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T15:52:54-07:00","id":1524156,"title":"","content":"Bumping my old thread. After some deliberation, I like the idea of the solars slowly chipping away at The Realm, forcing the dragon bloods to do something desperate and foolish...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T02:53:25-07:00","id":1524186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1524156#post1524156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bumping my old thread. After some deliberation, I like the idea of the solars slowly chipping away at The Realm, forcing the dragon bloods to do something desperate and foolish...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Nuke it from orbit. Its the only way to be sure. Full scorched earth of the cardinal directions.&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;Well congrats to whomever had that bright idea. Now since the Directions' population is mostly dead, the newest Solar exalts are now appearing on the blessed isle.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T18:12:07-07:00","id":1524341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1524156#post1524156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bumping my old thread. After some deliberation, I like the idea of the solars slowly chipping away at The Realm, forcing the dragon bloods to do something desperate and foolish...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, One of my favorite characters (&amp; game) was set in a Pre-Jade Prision break. It was tough to face against the un-weakenend might of the DB Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> Main question for you are there 300 Solars? or just 150 (with Abyssals and Infernals) ?<br /> \u200b<br /> Regarding desperate thing DB might do:<br /> <br /> Cast Captured Solars into the Underworld/Abyss or to Hell (Yozis) itself and then pull a pikachu face when Abyssals and Infernals come knocking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T19:24:54-07:00","id":1524346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1524341#post1524341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, One of my favorite characters (&amp; game) was set in a Pre-Jade Prision break. It was tough to face against the un-weakenend might of the DB Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> Main question for you are there 300 Solars? or just 150 (with Abyssals and Infernals) ?<br /> \u200b<br /> Regarding desperate thing DB might do:<br /> <br /> Cast Captured Solars into the Underworld/Abyss or to Hell (Yozis) itself and then pull a pikachu face when Abyssals and Infernals come knocking.</div> </div> </div> </div>i would assume that no, likely no Abyssals or Infernals... But never say Never! That idea is pretty wild, would the DB's actually go into the Underworld? But at the same time, I can see some desperate Sidereals doing such a thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T16:44:49-08:00","id":1528185,"title":"","content":"Initially it'd be a lot of dead Solars, then the Wyld Hunt would start getting stretched thin but also starts receiving regular funding from the Empress, because she and Chejob know this is NOT going away easily. Then there'd be a lot of tired and scared Dragonblooded and Sidereals, it'd settle into either a protracted internecine Exalted violence or a Cold War Scenario where both* sides are left wondering how many times can they fire the Realm Defense Grid without shaking the Blessed Isle to pieces or if they've got enough juice Perfect Parry it at this moment. It then settles into a game of Diplomacy, Espionage and Sabotage, Nations being built, absorbed and made to feed one side or another's burgeoning military industrial complex.<br /> Then the Mask of Winters pops out of The Underworld to take Thorns and gets attacked by several hundred different factions, a number of them accusing each other of working for him the ENTIRE time. Huzzah.<br /> <br /> *I'm oversimplifying, there will be more than two despite the best efforts of the largest concentration of Solars and the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T21:08:52-08:00","id":1528200,"title":"","content":"I'm not convinced the solars would necessarily be united, however, they very well could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T19:17:22-08:00","id":1528292,"title":"","content":"Over time a united solar faction would be possible, but I suspect it would likely be more of a sort of social contract sort of like how the silver pact seems to be this edition. You know everyone has their own objectives, but there are rules against infighting and procedures for helping newbies, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T04:31:32-08:00","id":1528411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1528200#post1528200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not convinced the solars would necessarily be united, however, they very well could be.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1528292#post1528292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over time a united solar faction would be possible, but I suspect it would likely be more of a sort of social contract sort of like how the silver pact seems to be this edition. You know everyone has their own objectives, but there are rules against infighting and procedures for helping newbies, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could definitely see a 'Solar Pact' situation arising as the most sensible option. Between the Great Curse, the fact Creation is a <i>much</i> smaller space following the Great Contagion, and the formation of the Silver Pact and how Lunars have changed since the Usurpation, I reckon any serious attempt to unify the Lawgivers into a single faction akin to the Solar Deliberative is only bound for catastrophic failure and infighting with a lot of collateral damage. There's no doubt that a few hundred Solars could destabilize, destroy, conquer etc. Yu-Shan and the Realm but it's the aftermath where things would fall apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T10:35:29-08:00","id":1528421,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean... <br /> <br /> Solars. To call them fractious, ambitious, and having the strongest integrity charms is an understatement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T13:36:07-08:00","id":1529172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress?p=1528200#post1528200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not convinced the solars would necessarily be united, however, they very well could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really matter. Some would go solo, some would form smaller groups (and some wight even go against each other), but Realm would need to deal with all of them all the same.<br /> <br /> From what i understand Dragonblooded are pretty much already stretched thin. They can send smaller kill teams, they can send an army somewhere (like they did dealing with Jochim, and later with the Bull), but sending <i>several</i> armies in <i>different</i> directions at the same time invites a possibility of getting Futile Blooded way too often. Even if they were to suffer a crushing defeat (or even a pyrrhic victory) just once every 30 to 50 years, in the long run it is a losing strategy.<br /> <br /> Besides, there's another aspect to it.If it's not a sustainable situation for the Realm as a whole, it's even less interesting for individual Houses. I mean, after the first House ends up the same way Tepets did in the original scenario, the next time an army needs to be sent another House might think twice about sending it too far away. And, sure, the Empress, still being present and in power can try to &quot;encourage&quot; her subjects to be more enthusiasting ebout doing their duties, but dragging feet (and trying to push the more dangerous assignments towards other houses) would still happen. And when dealing with Solars any kinds of delays can be deadly, because, in the end, the time is not on Dragonblooded's side.<br /> <br /> Now, in such a situation Sids would likely decide to become more active once again, but they aren't exactly unified either. And Lunars would almost certainly also try to capitalize on the situation as well. In the end, it would get definitely messy. Not as <i>immediately</i> messy as the canonical situation, but still equally bad in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 01-22-2024, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T11:49:43-08:00","id":1529830,"title":"","content":"You'd be looking at some 60 or so Civilizations that in the absolute best case scenario, will still give the Realm a headache putting down. And the ones who can push them back, or worst of all can keep things on the downlow until their Solar population (roughly 5 of them, some groups larger some smaller and a few loners just sort of wandering around) can not just survive a shot form the RGD, but retaliate with some Plagues of Egypt mojo, which coincidentally leaves their home base unscathed. This of course assumes it all happens in a vacuum and the Lunars aren't sitting back watching the show, eating popcorn. Between Solar Bonds, their collective grudge with the Realm and Sidereals and the Exalted tendency to push things as far as they can possibly go; this isn't likely and there'll be a lot of Lunars (though not quite 1:1 in Ex3) pulling up to offer their support.<br /> Given Lunar doctrine where Anti-Realm armies are concerned, they may or may not run out when it gets bad. I think there'll be a lot of annoyed but proud Elder Lunars watching their former wards lay down their lives alongside their new allies.<br /> Another important aspect of this is, unless somebody fucks around and finds out; there won't be any Abyssals or Infernals. The Deathlords are forced to act more directly and Hell remains in it's Extramarital Observation Shed, with some of the wilier figures taking advantage of the mounting desperation, you may start to see the Realm starting to field Terrestrials wielding elemental might not of Creation, but the Underworld or Malfeas; as they seek some edge against the various Solar Civs, who themselves might find themselves making a deal with the Devil to keep their people alive on those occasions where the Realm prevails. So there may indeed actually be some limited Infenral and Abyssal Activity, not at the same level of vanilla Exalted though.<br /> Meanwhile, up in the heaven; Sidereals are miserable. It's great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":".  needed bracketing and some proofreading, christ you'd think I'd work for Onyx Path. 02-01-2024, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}